== from behind, through 10 um of aluminium: absorbed in the foil alone 50 dB (skin depth 1.7 um), plus the reflection at its face; in practice the edges and seams decide
== from behind, through 20 um of aluminium: absorbed in the foil alone 101 dB (skin depth 1.7 um), plus the reflection at its face; in practice the edges and seams decide
== the thinnest a metal-backed absorber with no magnetic material can be (Rozanov's bound),
   for the two bands only, 2.4-2.5 and 5.15-5.85 GHz:
   -10 dB over both: at least 0.7 mm (a bound; reaching it takes a design, and it says nothing of how)
   -20 dB over both: at least 1.4 mm (a bound; reaching it takes a design, and it says nothing of how)
